WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:04.980
Goldfish Life

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:12.820
are forcing the Adnimoon Company to enact major operational changes.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.160
These air pirates have concentrated their efforts

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.120
on seizing the scarce amount of methane hydrate energy resources that remain untapped,

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:22.750
intending to ransom it back to the rest of the world at exorbitant prices.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.380
The entire industry has suffered immensely at their hands

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.590
and our company is now the only energy supplier left at operational capacity.

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:35.340
Needless to say,

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.350
this places a lot of responsibility on a single company like Adnimoon.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.230
On behalf of all of us at Adnimoon,

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:47.450
I pledge to you that we will continue to provide the world with a stable source of methane hydrate!

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.620
Amnesia?

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:08.290
Strange, isn't it?

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:11.130
She remembers her daily behaviors and retains all of her technical knowledge,

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:15.470
but she recalls nothing at all of her personal life.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.840
That does work to our advantage, though...

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:22.810
She doesn't remember that we attacked her daughters

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.440
and her intellect is still of use to us.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.480
She will continue working here as a valued employee.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:32.050
And now we just need the three sisters.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:35.110
The Galileo Tesoro is within our grasp.

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.860
I presume that there are no problems on your end?

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:39.650
Of course not.

00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:43.400
Leave it to Messier... And to me.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:02:01.600
koreijou kitai wa shinai to sakki kimeta no ni

00:01:50.380 --> 00:02:01.600
I decided that I won't have any more expectations

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:09.400
megakuramu juubyou ga sugireba

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:09.400
But when these dazzling ten seconds pass

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:16.650
sugu yuragu fukidashita yokan

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:16.650
I already feel like bursting into laughter

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.740
shinkuromanika

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:18.740
Synchromanica

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.280
itsu no ma ni ka

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:20.280
Before I know it

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.450
kono koe wa negai no you da

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.450
This voice starts to sound like a wish

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:29.750
tanjun ni ikanai mirai ga tokimeki no sumika

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:29.750
The future isn't simple, but it brings excitement

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:36.260
boku no mimi wa dareka no yume da

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:36.260
I can hear someone's dream

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:43.220
kotoba ni wa shinain da subete

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:43.220
But I won't say any of it out loud

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.030
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:56.030
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.360
shinkuromanika

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:58.360
Synchromanica

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.490
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:02.490
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.530
shinkuromanika

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.530
Synchromanica

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.750
kimi wa ikeru shinkuro

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.750
The synchrony of your life

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.980
I'm safe!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.730
I'm relieved to hear that your dad's okay.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.910
Well, I knew it would take more than that to kill him.

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:44.250
In any case,

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:47.990
this means that we can focus our efforts on locating Galileo's inheritance.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:52.620
Traveling with Galileo's descendants...
It's like a dream come true!

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.270
Galileo's inheritance, huh?

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:57.590
Good luck with that.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.250
Wait, how can you act like it doesn't concern you?

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:02.380
My target is right here.

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.640
To think that the famous Adnimoon Company was behind this...

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:09.970
And that they even have enough power to use the police to capture us...

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.430
That's not exactly right.

00:04:13.190 --> 00:04:16.440
Hazuki

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:16.440
The ones that attacked you belong to the group Messier.

00:04:17.050 --> 00:04:19.210
Adnimoon's darker side.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:22.190
It's a terrifying organization that operates in the shadows.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:24.410
It doesn't matter which side it is!

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:28.080
I can't let them use a large corporation as a front for illegal activity!

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:32.500
I will act in the name of law and justice and deliver a crushing blow!

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:35.030
I know how you feel,

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:37.290
but you shouldn't underestimate Messier.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:43.130
They attacked me several times during my search for the Galileo Tesoro.

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:46.510
And what I've learned about them has only confirmed just how terrifying they are.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:50.140
Then the sheer scope of their evil makes it all the more necessary to bring them down!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:51.520
C'mon now, Hazuki-chan...

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.560
Whatever. Stop complicating things!

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.940
If you aren't going to help, go away!

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:04.240
All of this... Hocchibi did all of this on her own?

00:05:06.930 --> 00:05:08.780
It reeks of oil.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:12.790
Hozuki-chan!

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:14.500
About Galileo's inheritance—

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.370
I'm sorry, Anna-san,

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.890
I have to fetch some parts.

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.300
Wasn't that a little rude?

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.590
Kazuki-chan!

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:29.570
Sorry!

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:34.450
This sucks...

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:35.870
Are you okay?

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:40.850
What are you doing in here?

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:42.250
Nothing, really.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:43.980
But isn't this amazing?

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:49.110
She clearly accounted for everything while designing the flotation components.

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:54.240
Subtle details like that are what really
distinguish you girls as descendants of Galileo.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:57.090
I guess so...

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:59.380
For example, those scales really stand out.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:02.360
At first glance they seem purely decorative,

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:05.440
but they actually generate lift.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:06.380
I don't get it.

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:07.470
Huh?

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:10.840
I don't understand that sort of thing, so...

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:15.120
Did I strike a nerve?

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:22.440
That's it. I'm at my limit.

00:06:24.250 --> 00:06:25.480
No way.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:29.070
Oh, Hocchii.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.530
Nice timing.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.070
Do you have any food?

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:33.120
Food?

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.580
Preferably fit for human consumption.

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.190
It reeks of oil.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:46.240
Really, what am I doing here?

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:55.530
I want to go home...

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.200
I've been waiting for you.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:01.400
Anna-san?

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:04.800
The <i>Galileo</i> truly is remarkable.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:07.280
I can't believe you made this all alone.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.150
You're a genuine descendant of Galileo Galilei!

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:11.480
Um...

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:14.910
Is the ship's name final?

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:16.240
Not necessarily.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:19.460
I think it's fine.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:20.770
The <i>Galileo</i>...

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:21.890
Right?

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:22.880
Yes!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:27.340
I had no idea you'd created an autopilot function as well.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.510
Grande Rosso operates it.

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:33.720
Nice to meet you!

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.640
It talks?

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:39.080
Grande Rosso is an AI I made.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.810
She's my friend.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:45.120
She could've at least stocked the rooms with a little beer and some snacks...

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:47.430
Hocchii's so inconsiderate.

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.910
Wh-Wh-What?

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.360
Sorry, my mistake.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:57.120
I guess the kitchen's next door...

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.490
It isn't easy finding your way around...

00:07:58.490 --> 00:07:59.950
There should really be a sign or something.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:01.420
Who would make that mistake?

00:08:01.420 --> 00:08:02.890
Wait, it was deliberate, wasn't it?

00:08:02.890 --> 00:08:05.330
Whatever, just shut the door!

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:07.000
Why are you so flustered?

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.170
We're both girls.

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:09.340
Sisters, even.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:12.010
That isn't the issue, you idiot!

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:15.280
I think I heard something.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:16.850
You probably imagined it.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:18.390
More importantly, Hozuki,

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:20.720
where is the <i>Galileo</i> headed?

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:23.600
I have not determined a destination at present.

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:27.170
Since picking up Hozuki-chan and her sisters, I've been flying in a straight line.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.020
I see.

00:08:29.020 --> 00:08:31.110
Then escape is our current priority.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:33.150
But that's not a long term plan...

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:35.130
I know!

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:38.160
I think Papa might've been right.

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:42.240
If the enemy's after Galileo's secrets,

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:44.960
you three should be the ones to discover them.

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:49.160
That isn't the only reason, but...

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:54.140
But I've made up my mind.

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:55.510
I...

00:08:55.510 --> 00:08:56.800
Ow...

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.260
Damn Kakkii.

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:01.270
Seriously?

00:09:02.290 --> 00:09:03.770
I don't have...

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:05.530
any clean underwear.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:11.440
I will look for Galileo's inheritance.

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:14.830
I will never give in to evil!

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:21.620
I want to go home!

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:30.880
Here.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:33.380
What's this?

00:09:33.740 --> 00:09:35.780
It's a walkie-talkie.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:40.180
They can tap cell phone transmissions, so we can't use those anymore.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:42.570
You made these?

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:44.990
So quickly? Amazing!

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:48.560
Haa-nee, Kaa-nee, give me your phones.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.140
Why?

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:53.860
If we keep our cell phones,
the enemy might be able to find us...

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:55.360
So we need to get rid of them.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:56.960
Mine too, of course.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:09:57.900
Huh?

00:09:57.900 --> 00:10:00.910
Hmm, I guess there's no getting around it.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:02.240
Here.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.120
You too, Kakkii.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.780
N-No.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:08.120
Kaa-nee?

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:10.380
Wh-Why do we have to get rid of them?

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:13.420
There must be another way.
Can't we just turn them off?

00:10:13.650 --> 00:10:17.240
No, I think Hozuki-chan is right.

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:18.680
Even if you turn it off,

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:23.310
there are still ways to learn the location
using IC cards and satellites.

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:25.810
You're saying they'd go that far?

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:28.810
Is there any guarantee they won't?

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:30.810
What the hell?

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:35.330
Why do we need walkie-talkies, anyway?!

00:10:35.330 --> 00:10:36.490
Well,

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:39.730
when you do any kind of traveling,
you obviously need a way to communicate.

00:10:39.730 --> 00:10:40.480
Traveling?

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:43.500
That reminds me! Hocchii, the fridge is empty.

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:45.200
Seems we'll be on the road for a while.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.200
We should stock up on food somewhere.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:49.360
Yeah, I know.

00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:53.130
Grande Rosso, could you find me the closest city?

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:55.730
Okay! Search commencing.

00:10:55.730 --> 00:10:57.090
It'll be just a second.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.460
Guys, listen to yourselves.

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:00.470
Just listen to—

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.340
It's going to be okay, Kazuki-chan.

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:06.800
Not only did Hozuki-chan build the <i>Galileo</i> despite her age,

00:11:06.800 --> 00:11:10.620
but you and Hazuki-chan are also here.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:13.860
With three of Galileo Galilei's descendants on board,

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:16.610
we're certain to find a way through this!

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:19.860
Can you just stop with the whole descendant thing?

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:22.060
There's no need to be modest.

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:24.290
You only need one look at this machine

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:29.620
to know that you three are the real thing...
True descendants of Galileo.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:30.620
I...

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:32.680
The search is complete!

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:36.380
We will be able to safely procure supplies in none of the surrounding urban areas!

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:38.800
Huh? Why not?

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:40.880
This seems to be the reason.

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:46.200
Huh?!

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:54.300
Huh? Is this déjà vu?

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:56.060
Don't look, pervert.

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.570
I'd like to take a shower.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:58.440
Could you move?

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:00.940
I want to be alone.

00:12:01.380 --> 00:12:04.140
Kakkii, what's eating you?

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:05.930
I'm not a real one...

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:08.740
I can't make walkie-talkies or mechas like this.

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:09.330
I can't.

00:12:09.810 --> 00:12:11.080
What are you talking about?

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.410
Hocchibi's crazy.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:17.540
How can she consider actually looking for Galileo's inheritance in a situation like this?

00:12:17.540 --> 00:12:22.010
She isn't thinking about us at all.

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:27.510
Come with me for a minute.

00:12:28.780 --> 00:12:31.890
This ship has plenty of tableware, but no food at all.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:34.190
Hocchii misses things like that, sometimes.

00:12:34.860 --> 00:12:36.400
So, notice anything here?

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:37.770
Like what?

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:42.340
The dishes that are here... There are five of each.

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:46.030
Salad plates, dinner plates, forks, knives, everything...

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:49.230
Enough for our whole family.

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:50.410
Kazuki

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:53.540
Those are apparently Japanese letters.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:55.920
Five beds, too...

00:12:55.920 --> 00:13:01.550
If she hadn't been thinking of us at all,
do you think she would've done all this?

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:07.590
I think she made the walkie-talkies so that we could keep track of each other too.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:31.120
Today's catch: goldfish.

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:33.600
What was that impact just now?

00:13:36.410 --> 00:13:37.040
That's...

00:13:37.820 --> 00:13:38.880
An Aza Iron!

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.630
It's coming! We have to intercept it!

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:42.740
Huh?

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:43.630
Um...

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.810
Those moves totally break the rules!

00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:01.310
Reverse!

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.030
I can't!

00:14:14.550 --> 00:14:17.730
Greetings, Galileo Sisters...

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:18.710
That voice...

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:22.250
I'm honored to meet you.

00:14:22.700 --> 00:14:24.140
You know him?

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:26.880
Didn't you see him on the laptop earlier?

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:29.260
He's the heir to the Adnimoon Company,

00:14:29.780 --> 00:14:31.740
Roberto Materrazzi.

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:34.220
I don't like to beat around the bush,

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:36.470
so I'll get right to the point.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:39.050
Hand over the Galileo Tesoro.

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:40.150
If you refuse...

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:44.150
He'll crush us.

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:48.900
Hocchii! Get us out of here!

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:51.200
I'm trying, but...

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:54.580
I can't deal with this...

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:57.170
Why do we have to go through this?

00:14:57.170 --> 00:14:59.710
We don't know anything about the Galileo Tesoro!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:01.710
Well? Your answer?

00:15:07.490 --> 00:15:08.340
That's...

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:12.280
This is...

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:16.060
The Moon sketch!

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.600
Wait, what?

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:19.060
You didn't know?

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:22.160
It's a sketch Galileo was said to have left behind.

00:15:22.160 --> 00:15:26.020
If we can find more clues like this,
they should lead us to the Galileo Tesoro!

00:15:26.310 --> 00:15:28.030
Hozuki-chan, this...

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:32.030
Your answer?

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:34.660
Let's just give him the sketch!

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:37.620
We aren't giving it to him.

00:15:37.620 --> 00:15:39.870
Haa-nee? Why?

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:43.370
If the enemy wants this, we can't let them have it.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:44.790
It's our trump card.

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:45.880
Huh?

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:47.160
What are you talking about?

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:48.670
What do you mean, trump card?

00:15:48.670 --> 00:15:51.200
If we hand it over, we won't be targeted anymore.

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:52.890
We can go home!

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:56.280
We're international fugitives now, remember?

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:58.180
You still think we can go home?

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:01.480
Wouldn't that change once we give up the drawing?

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:03.690
No... We aren't giving it to him.

00:16:03.990 --> 00:16:04.930
Huh?

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:08.190
We can't give him anything important, not ever!

00:16:08.430 --> 00:16:10.740
How can you say that in a situation like this?!

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.150
Take a look around you!

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:13.780
There is no other way!

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:14.780
There is.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:15.870
There must be!

00:16:16.450 --> 00:16:17.650
You...

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:19.540
You're having so much fun right now, aren't you?

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:22.910
Building some super machine like this, saving us

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:24.040
and just being great at everything.

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:27.920
And if we started traveling,
you'd get to show off your talents even more!

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:29.300
I bet you're excited!

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:31.050
I wasn't thinking that—

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:32.730
Just shut up, already!

00:16:32.730 --> 00:16:35.580
That sketch is what they're after...

00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:37.890
Once we hand it over, we can be done.

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:39.310
We won't be done!

00:16:39.650 --> 00:16:41.620
They've made us international fugitives,

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:44.450
and now they're even chasing us with that weapon.

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:47.690
You think that if we hand this over,
they'll just say "Thank you!" and let us go?

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:50.300
What's their deal, anyway?

00:16:50.300 --> 00:16:52.320
It's either us or them.

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:54.720
There's no easy way out!

00:16:54.720 --> 00:16:56.320
This is insane.

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:59.280
Hocchibi, Haa-nee...
You're not making any sense!

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:00.080
Kazuki-chan!

00:17:13.020 --> 00:17:15.180
Everything reeks of oil...

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:18.300
I can smell Hozuki everywhere!

00:17:31.430 --> 00:17:32.950
What should we do?

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:34.490
Pirates

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:43.160
The air pirates' <i>Black Ganymede</i>?

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:44.640
That mecha!

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.370
Yo! We meet again!

00:17:47.370 --> 00:17:49.020
Unfortunately,

00:17:49.020 --> 00:17:52.210
we have first dibs on Galileo's inheritance.

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:57.220
I don't want you hyena bastards and your filthy paws anywhere near it!

00:17:57.650 --> 00:18:00.470
And what can a lowly band of air pirates do?

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.060
You're just a rich boy who's never seen a hard day.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:06.480
Let me show you a bit of the real world.

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:17.650
I'll turn you into a real man!

00:18:26.540 --> 00:18:28.220
Hocchii, now!

00:18:28.220 --> 00:18:29.040
Okay!

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:37.980
Not bad, Bambina!

00:18:37.980 --> 00:18:40.400
Boss, it's a little early to be laughing...

00:18:40.400 --> 00:18:41.840
They're getting away!

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:01.490
That was quite entertaining.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:05.160
I'll withdraw... At least for today.

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:42.340
"That summer, due to your sudden appearance,

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:46.280
"I learned about an emotion unique to humanity,

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:48.750
"that terribly ambiguous, abstract notion

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:52.730
"known as love, which is subject to neither proof nor verification."

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:56.290
Getting saved by air pirates ticks me off!

00:19:56.730 --> 00:20:02.530
You know about the worldwide attacks on methane hydrate mining sites, right?

00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:04.550
Yeah, but why bring that up now?

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:07.240
Adnimoon is behind the attacks.

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:10.850
They're using Messier to steal energy resources from other companies,

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:12.810
to increase their market share.

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:14.410
Seriously?

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:15.600
Super seriously.

00:20:15.600 --> 00:20:18.570
And they're blaming it all on air pirates.

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:21.570
So that's why he called them "hyena bastards."

00:20:23.980 --> 00:20:27.810
I guess I can understand why air pirates would see obtaining the Galileo Tesoro

00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:30.910
as the best way to oppose Messier.

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:34.170
Right, they're looking at the bigger picture.

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:38.540
But we don't know where the other sketches

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:40.780
that lead to the Tesoro are, do we?

00:20:40.780 --> 00:20:42.420
That would be the problem.

00:20:43.230 --> 00:20:45.680
There must be a hint somewhere, but...

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.660
No leads on that?

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:50.680
Maybe something related to Galileo holds a clue...

00:20:51.130 --> 00:20:53.600
Oh! If you keep telling us Galileo trivia,

00:20:53.600 --> 00:20:55.800
maybe we'll hit the jackpot.

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:58.490
Let's see, Galileo trivia...

00:20:58.490 --> 00:20:59.580
For example,

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:03.190
when he was growing up, Galileo studied music.

00:21:03.190 --> 00:21:05.250
Stuff like that?

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:07.320
Maybe that was too much like common knowledge.

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:09.700
I had no idea...

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:11.920
But that's totally irrelevant.

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:14.080
Music...

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:14.830
What?

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:16.830
There's something...

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:19.190
here.

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
asa ga kuru no mo kizukanai mama

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:41.070
I used to not even notice the sun rising

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
nagareboshi wo sagashiteta

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:44.900
As I was looking for shooting stars

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
ano koro no you ni sora wo miageru koto mo shinakunatteta

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:51.910
But now I no longer look up at the sky like that

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
nande mo nai negaigoto datte

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:57.040
I don't even remember the wishes I wanted to make

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
hitori ja nai kono basho nara

00:21:57.040 --> 00:22:01.420
That place where I'm not alone

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
kitto mata mitsukedaseru

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:06.720
I'm sure I can find it again

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
ima yozora ni kagayaku hoshikuzu no naka kara

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:14.680
Among the stardust shining in the night sky

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
wasurekakete ita itsuka no mirai wo sagasou

00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:23.070
I'll search for the future that I had almost forgotten

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
me wo korashite hitosuji no hikari ga

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:30.200
As I strain my eyes to find that single beam of light

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
oto mo naku nagareru sono kiseki oikakete yukou

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:42.340
I'll chase after that silently flowing miracle
